&lt;li&gt;Experience with guardrails or monitoring for AI systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in fintech, payments or another regulated industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Startup experience, especially at an AI-native company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of our total compensation package that also includes benefits and equity. Pay decisions are based on a number of factors, including scope and qualifications for the role, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Coast employees. We expect the majority of candidates who are offered roles at Coast to fall healthily within the range based on these factors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary range&lt;/strong&gt;: $150,000 - $180,000 annually&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity Grant&lt;/strong&gt;: Meaningful potential upside given Coast’s early-stage trajectory&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits Overview&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental and vision insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible paid time off (vacation, personal well being, paid holidays)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tools to help manage your financial wellness, including webinars, access to an equity tax advisory service, and company-sponsored 401(k)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$400 accessories allowance (a keyboard, mouse, headphones, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free lunch every Friday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coast is committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion. We are building a diverse and inclusive environment, so we encourage people of all backgrounds to apply. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check out the latest podcast interview on&lt;a href=&quot;https://fintechlayercake.buzzsprout.com/1985266/14997028-fleet-card-masterclass-with-coast-founder-daniel-simon&quot;&gt; Fintech Layer Cake with Coast Founder Daniel Simon&lt;/a&gt;!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://boards.greenhouse.io/coast/jobs/coastpay.com&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Coast&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; is re-imagining the trillion-dollar U.S. B2B card payments infrastructure, with a focus on the country’s 500,000 commercial fleets, 40 million commercial vehicles, and many million commercial drivers. The incumbent technologies that cater to these customers are decades old, and drivers and fleets increasingly demand modern digital experiences and affordable and transparent financial services products. Coast&#39;s mission is to deliver them at a transformational scale, beginning with the Coast Fleet and Fuel Card built on a cutting-edge spend management platform.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;As a member of our founding BDR team in our new Utah office, you will play the most crucial part of the sales lifecycle, being the first point of contact for prospective customers. Armed with a suite of business-critical SaaS tools, you will proactively engage with new prospects - sparking interest, uncovering pain points and qualifying if Coast is a fit for their business (on most occasions we are an ideal fit!).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are hiring for our newest west coast office in Draper, UT.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospect for, generate and qualify leads to create sales-ready opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make outbound (cold) calls and emails daily.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Research and prospect ideal customers and gather key lead information through open-ended questions and thoughtful conversations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceed monthly quotas of qualified appointments/demos scheduled and deals closed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Work closely with the Account Executives and the rest of the sales team to accelerate the sales cycle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pipeline management: enter and maintain data in Salesforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Represent Coast with integrity and professionalism at all times in all written and oral communications while highlighting Coast’s value proposition and key selling points to raise interest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;1+ years of experience is sales or a customer facing role, B2B experience preferred.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree from a 4 years college or university&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills - written and verbal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are confident, well-spoken and driven.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Attention to detail, organizational skills, and fantastic with time management.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience carrying and exceeding KPI’s and targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience in customer facing roles such as retail, hospitality or customer service and are keen to explore a career in tech sales.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;An enthusiasm for entrepreneurship and creativity! This might be the single most important point.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Critically, you must be practical and business-minded, smart and creative, and excited about the rewards and volatility of an early-stage venture-backed startup.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;ll bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real growth and career development opportunities, we’re still young in Utah with plenty of room to grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A unique product that makes an actual impact on the businesses we serve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attractive base and commissions package - uncapped earnings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Medical, dental and vision insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Flexible paid time off (vacation, personal well being, paid holidays)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Tools to help manage your financial wellness, including webinars, access to an equity tax advisory service, and company-sponsored 401(k)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;$400 accessories allowance (a keyboard, mouse, headphones, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Education stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Free lunch every Friday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coast&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;will not&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;sponsorship to work in the United States for this role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Coast&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coast is co-founded and led by Daniel Simon, who previously cofounded Bread (breadpayments.com), a leading payments and credit technology firm backed by some of the world’s top VCs which was acquired for $500MM+ in 2020.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Coast has raised $165M in total funding — our recent &lt;a href=&quot;https://techcrunch.com/2024/07/18/fintech-startup-coast-lands-40m-just-4-months-after-its-last-25m-raise/&quot;&gt;$40M Series B equity round was led by ICONIQ Growth&lt;/a&gt; with participation from Thomvest, and Synchrony. We&#39;re also backed by top fintech and mobility venture funds – including Accel, Insight Partners, Better Tomorrow Ventures, Avid Ventures, Bessemer Venture Partners, BoxGroup, Foundation Capital, Greycroft, Colle – and premier angel investors – including Max Levchin (Affirm), Josh Abramowitz (Bread), Jason Gardner (Marqeta), William Hockey (Plaid), Ryan Petersen (Flexport), and many others.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check out the latest podcast interview on &lt;a href=&quot;https://fintechlayercake.buzzsprout.com/1985266/14997028-fleet-card-masterclass-with-coast-founder-daniel-simon&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Fintech Layer Cake with Coast Founder Daniel Simon&lt;/a&gt;!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coast is committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion. We are building a diverse and inclusive environment, so we encourage people of all backgrounds to apply. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is Coast&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coast is re-imagining the trillion-dollar U.S. B2B card payments infrastructure, with a focus on the country’s 500,000 commercial fleets, 40 million commercial vehicles, and many millions of commercial drivers. The incumbent technologies that cater to these customers are decades old, and businesses with fleets increasingly demand modern digital experiences and transparent financial services products. Coast’s mission is to deliver this at a transformational scale, beginning with the Coast Fleet and Fuel Card built on a cutting-edge spend management platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coast’s biggest initiatives cross every team. You’ll own them: get the right people aligned, keep the work moving, and make sure it lands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Business Operations Associate, that someone is you. You’ll own and run cross-functional projects tied to Coast’s top priorities, from first scoping to final handoff. You’ll work with leaders across the company, so you’ll need to be credible with executives and just as comfortable in the details with the people doing the work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is a big part of how we do this. You’ll use it to plan faster, synthesize information, draft and analyze, and automate the repetitive parts of project work. You’ll also run projects that put AI to use across the business. You don’t need to be an engineer. You do need to be the person who reaches for AI first, and who can tell when it’s doing a good job and when it isn’t.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone who gets energy from turning an ambiguous goal into a clear plan, getting a dozen people aligned, and shipping. You’ll be expected to act like an owner: you take responsibility for the outcome, not just your piece of it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s a generalist role with broad exposure to how a growth-stage fintech runs. Over time, you can build depth in an area you care about and take on bigger parts of the business as it scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own cross-functional projects end to end&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run company-level and cross-team initiatives from scoping through launch: define the goal, build the plan, line up owners, set milestones, and drive it to done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep projects moving across teams that don’t report to you. You get things unstuck by making the next step obvious and the tradeoffs clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot risks and dependencies early, raise them with a recommendation, and keep leaders informed without making them chase you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close projects properly: document what shipped, what you learned, and what happens next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the connective tissue across the company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product, Sales, Finance, Risk, Legal, People, and Operations to make sure the right people are in the room and decisions get made.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate between teams. Take a goal from an executive and break it into work others can act on, and take messy ground-level input and turn it into something leadership can decide on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the cadences that keep cross-functional work on track: kickoffs, standups, status updates, and retros.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support quarterly planning and goal tracking by turning priorities into projects with owners and dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help figure out what we should do next&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope and evaluate new opportunities, such as a new process, partnership, or initiative, and bring leaders a clear recommendation backed by the numbers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the analyses and decision frameworks that help leadership prioritize and decide where to put time and money.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ideas from “this could work” to a pilot, then to something the company runs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use AI to move faster and to help the company use it&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI in your own project work: planning, synthesizing inputs from many teams, drafting, analysis, and status reporting. Build repeatable workflows and prompts that cut the manual work out of running a project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run projects that bring AI into how Coast operates, from piloting a new tool to redesigning a process around automation, and measure whether it worked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate new AI tools against real problems and give a clear recommendation on what we should adopt and what we should skip.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share what works. Write it down and teach other teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring data to the decisions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define what success looks like for each project and track it with real numbers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pull and analyze data to size problems, test assumptions, and measure results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build simple, clear updates and dashboards that show leaders where a project stands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By 30 days&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know the company’s current priorities, the key leaders, and how decisions get made.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve taken over one active project and the people on it know you’re the person to go to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By 90 days&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve run a cross-functional project from start to finish, and the teams involved would work with you again.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leaders get clear, regular project updates from you and don’t need to ask where things stand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve used AI to take real time out of how you run projects, and you can show how.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By 6 months&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re running multiple projects at once without things slipping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve led at least one project that put AI to work in the business, with a measured result.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executives trust you with high-priority, high-visibility work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teams use the project templates, cadences, and playbooks you built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-4 years in business operations, project or program management, strategy and operations, consulting, or a similar role. Fintech, SaaS, or financial services is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of running cross-functional projects with many stakeholders and shipping them on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native mindset: you already use AI tools in your daily work, you’ve built something with them (a workflow, an automation, an agent, a prompt library), and you’re excited to push further.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong structured thinking: you can take an ambiguous problem and turn it into a clear plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication. You can brief an executive in two minutes and write the doc that gets a team aligned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical instincts: comfortable with data, spreadsheets, and spotting trends, and able to turn them into a recommendation. SQL and low-code tools are a plus, and you’re willing to learn them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership mindset: you spot problems before they’re assigned and drive them to done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of moving fast and finding smarter ways to reach the outcome, and teammates who’d gladly work with you again.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and process-driven; able to juggle multiple projects and priorities in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable influencing without authority and working with people at every level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you don’t match every requirement, apply anyway. We care most about how you think and how you deliver.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Get&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real ownership. You’ll run projects tied to the company’s top priorities, with your name on the outcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working time with leaders across the company, and a front-row view of how a growth-stage fintech makes decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on AI work. You’ll use it every day and help decide how the whole company uses it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A fast path to more scope as you prove yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of our total compensation package that also includes benefits and equity. Pay decisions are based on a number of factors, including scope and qualifications for the role, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Coast employees. We expect the majority of candidates who are offered roles at Coast to fall healthily within the range based on these factors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary range: $85,000 - $110,000 annually&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Equity Grant: Meaningful potential upside given Coast’s early-stage trajectory&lt;/p&gt;
