&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is Coast&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coast is re-imagining the trillion-dollar U.S. B2B card payments infrastructure, with a focus on the country’s 500,000 commercial fleets, 40 million commercial vehicles, and many millions of commercial drivers. The incumbent technologies that cater to these customers are decades old, and businesses with fleets increasingly demand modern digital experiences and transparent financial services products. Coast’s mission is to deliver this at a transformational scale, beginning with the Coast Fleet and Fuel Card built on a cutting-edge spend management platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we scale our Partnerships function, you will own the critical work of establishing strategic partnerships that drive the distribution of Coast’s product. Coast is built to help trades and transportation businesses save time and money, and you will identify, develop, and close relationships with prospective partners with whom we can share and drive that vision forward. This channel is growing very quickly and we’re excited to drive significant growth and innovation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Coast’s Head of Partnerships, CEO, and exec team to shape new partnership strategies for Coast to unlock at-scale distribution and create customer value through a variety of commercial relationships maintained by trades and transportation businesses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a pipeline: prioritize targets and build a prospecting plan to reach and engage potential partners for both distribution and customer value creation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute against your strategy, build relationships, and structure deals to drive increased distribution of Coast to new businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate deals with attractive economics, based on a mutual understanding of our and our partners core business models, in collaboration with finance and executive functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with legal to negotiate and close agreements by establishing a repeatable and scalable deal framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross functionally internally and externally to stand up partnerships and manage them to measurable success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think creatively to identify new partnership constructs for distribution, customer value, and driver/employee engagement - and quickly pressure test them for viability, demonstrating real innovation in GTM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work to activate partnerships, and sometimes wholly own marketing initiatives, including collateral, webinars, sales activation and even direct sales and customer engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend tradeshows and industry events to drive partnerships forward and activate current book of partnerships&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage partnerships: Maintain healthy partner relationships and drive towards long term strategic goals - in our current structure you will own and continue to activate and drive your partnerships forward&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your first year, you’ll be successful if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increase the number of active partnerships driving meaningful acquisition and payment for Coast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive meaningful growth in deals sold and onboarded through partner teams rather than just referral to Coast’s sales organization, contributing to lower payback period for Coast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and unlock distribution for Coast through new partner verticals, signing net new strategic deals for the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that the partnerships you structure drive healthy margins and profitability levels in addition to accelerating top-line revenue growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree from a four year university&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 3 - 7 years of experience in business development or partner management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise sales and partner enablement experience strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in vertical SaaS, field services trades, fleet management, financial services (including payments), or venture backed technology companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding executive presence and communication skills, for both internal and external audiences at all levels.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native mindset: you&#39;re already using AI tools in your daily work and you&#39;re excited to push further.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical instincts - comfortable pulling metrics, spotting trends, and translating data into operational and commercial decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience negotiating deals from indicative commercials through legal review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales and pitching toolkit: you can prospect, qualify, demonstrate, negotiate, and close deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excitement about jumping into an early stage, fast-growing company where we’re building the ship and sailing it at the same time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility and capability to navigate complex environments and ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General business acumen - understanding of complex business and revenue models and how to navigate “big picture” challenges with tactical strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of our total compensation package that also includes benefits and equity. Pay decisions are based on a number of factors, including scope and qualifications for the role, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Coast employees. We expect the majority of candidates who are offered roles at Coast to fall healthily within the range based on these factors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Total Compensation (Salary + Bonus) Range&lt;/strong&gt;: $160,000 – $195,000 annually&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity Grant&lt;/strong&gt;: Meaningful potential upside given Coast’s early-stage trajectory&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits Overview&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental and vision insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible paid time off (vacation, personal well being, paid holidays)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tools to help manage your financial wellness, including webinars, access to an equity tax advisory service, and company-sponsored 401(k)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$400 accessories allowance (a keyboard, mouse, headphones, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free lunch every Friday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coast is committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion. We are building a diverse and inclusive environment, so we encourage people of all backgrounds to apply. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check out the latest podcast interview on&lt;a href=&quot;https://fintechlayercake.buzzsprout.com/1985266/14997028-fleet-card-masterclass-with-coast-founder-daniel-simon&quot;&gt; Fintech Layer Cake with Coast Founder Daniel Simon&lt;/a&gt;!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is Coast&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coast is re-imagining the trillion-dollar U.S. B2B card payments infrastructure, with a focus on the country’s 500,000 commercial fleets, 40 million commercial vehicles, and many millions of commercial drivers. The incumbent technologies that cater to these customers are decades old, and businesses with fleets increasingly demand modern digital experiences and transparent financial services products. Coast’s mission is to deliver this at a transformational scale, beginning with the Coast Fleet and Fuel Card built on a cutting-edge spend management platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coast builds payments and spend management for fleet businesses: fuel cards, corporate cards and bill pay. We’re becoming AI-native: AI handles the repeatable work, so people can focus on customers and the hardest problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our sales team already runs on AI workflows we built in-house. Now we&#39;re building a small internal AI team to take that across the whole company. You&#39;ll join as one of two AI Operations Engineers, reporting to our AI Lead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a builder role with an operator’s mindset. You’ll find the highest-leverage work across Sales, Customer Success, Marketing, Support, Finance, Risk, Product, and Operations, and own it end to end, from first conversation to production. Some weeks you’ll write code; others you’ll run a workshop or redesign a process with a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Everyone at Coast uses Claude and builds their own skills. You build what they can’t: autonomous agents, and the foundation that makes everyone’s skills better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your first six months, you’ll ship three or more agents that teams rely on daily, each backed by evals that show it improving month over month. You’ll drive measurable gains in Coast’s operating efficiency, tracked in hours saved.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Find and prioritize the work.&lt;/strong&gt; Sit with teams, map their workflows, and size the time saved. Turn what you find into a ranked backlog with the AI Lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build autonomous agents.&lt;/strong&gt; Ship event-driven agents that do multi-step work across our stack. You’ll own the engineering off-the-shelf tools can’t do:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Loop and orchestration:&lt;/strong&gt; design agent loops, sub-agent handoffs, and when to act alone or escalate to a human.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Memory and context:&lt;/strong&gt; model shared memory as a knowledge graph, and decide what each agent sees, remembers and forgets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custom tooling:&lt;/strong&gt; build the tools our agents need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Traces and evals:&lt;/strong&gt; trace every run, score outputs against test sets built from real outcomes, and prove each version beats the last.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure impact.&lt;/strong&gt; Define success metrics for each build, track adoption and time saved, and report results to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run what you ship.&lt;/strong&gt; Own reliability, latency and cost in production, and catch regressions before users do. Partner with Security and IT on access, audit trails and the handling of sensitive data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable the company.&lt;/strong&gt; An AI-native company runs on self-service, and self-service needs solid infrastructure. You’ll architect the shared foundation the rest of Coast builds on: knowledge bases, application databases, templates, tools, and connectors. Then you’ll help people use it through training, office hours and hackathons, and grow a network of AI champions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay on the cutting edge.&lt;/strong&gt; Try new models and tools as they land, measure them against what we run today, and keep raising the bar on everything you’ve built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Projects you might take on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomous product help docs.&lt;/strong&gt; Build a brain that captures questions from customers (support tickets and calls) and employees (Slack). It spots missing or outdated articles, drafts updates, sends them for review, and learns from what gets approved and shared with customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal coach for large trials.&lt;/strong&gt; Build an agent that creates value calculators and tailored pitch decks from call transcripts and account data. It coaches AEs and CSMs through each trial with next steps, and learns which plays win.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–5 years in operations, product, solutions or forward-deployed engineering, internal tools, or a similar role at a fast-moving company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of shipping AI workflows or automations that people use every day. Show us what you built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on fluency with Claude Code, Cursor or similar coding agents, plus LLM tooling such as prompt design, tool use and MCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built at least one agent with persistent memory or a feedback loop that made it better over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with evals: building test sets, scoring outputs and using the results to improve an agent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort writing and reading code: SQL, plus Python or TypeScript scripting, APIs and webhooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication with non-technical teammates. You can teach as well as build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency: you spot inefficient processes and fix them without waiting to be asked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A software engineering background.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building with the MCP servers or APIs for tools like Salesforce, Notion, Slack and Gmail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with guardrails or monitoring for AI systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in fintech, payments or another regulated industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Startup experience, especially at an AI-native company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of our total compensation package that also includes benefits and equity. Pay decisions are based on a number of factors, including scope and qualifications for the role, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Coast employees. We expect the majority of candidates who are offered roles at Coast to fall healthily within the range based on these factors.&lt;/p&gt;
