&lt;h3 data-heading=&quot;At Coast, we&#39;re building the financial infrastructure powering America&#39;s fleets. AI is fundamentally changing how fleets run their financial operations, and we&#39;re shaping the tools this new era requires.&quot;&gt;At Coast, we&#39;re building the financial infrastructure powering America&#39;s fleets. AI is fundamentally changing how fleets run their financial operations, and we&#39;re shaping the tools this new era requires.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2020, Coast has become the payments and expense management platform of choice for the 500,000 fleets and 40 million vehicles that keep the country moving — giving fleet owners and operators control, visibility, and trust over how their businesses spend.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Simplicity is our competitive advantage. In an industry where complexity is the norm, we&#39;re building something opinionated and focused: software that field workers and fleet managers actually want to use. Every member of our fully co-located team is a builder who cares deeply about bringing modern, well-crafted tools to the trades — an industry that&#39;s been underserved for too long. This mindset drives everything we do, from product decisions to hiring choices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a senior to staff level Product Designer to join the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, we expect robust design skills, sharp product thinking, and the ability to engage in technical discussions. We work in small, autonomous project teams, where designers are paired tightly with engineers and product managers to explore ideas, build prototypes, deploy internal builds, and ultimately ship to customers. You will be a key element of projects from beginning to end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-heading=&quot;Location &amp;amp; work mode&quot;&gt;Location &amp;amp; work mode&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coast is an in-person company. This role is based out of our New York City office, where our full team works together day to day. We believe great products are built by people who are in the room together — collaborating closely, moving fast, and holding each other to a high bar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-heading=&quot;What you&#39;ll do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pair closely with engineering and product to initiate and complete roadmap projects, no hand-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot opportunities to redesign or refine key screens and flows, as well as smaller quality issues and “paper cuts” as you use Coast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create mockups, prototypes, and high-fidelity visuals to communicate ideas and describe their execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide and inspire fellow designers through collaborative critique of work-in-progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use and improve our lightweight design system components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help with hiring new teammates that can elevate our team and product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-heading=&quot;What we’re looking for&quot;&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years experience designing software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Courage to ask questions, experiment, and advocate for what you feel is right&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Humility to accept feedback, adapt your thinking, and iterate toward the best solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with prototyping in Figma (and beyond with tools like AI, HTML/CSS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to distill problems and feedback, then design clear, focused solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective written and verbal communication skills&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-heading=&quot;What we offer&quot;&gt;What we offer&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll have a high-impact role with real ownership and the opportunity to shape the future of Coast’s products and services&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary ($180,000—$220,000 USD) and equity&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-sponsored 401(k)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible paid time off (vacation, personal well being, paid holidays)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$400 accessories allowance (a keyboard, mouse, headphones, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tools to help manage your financial wellness, including webinar, and access to an equity tax advisory service&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free lunch on Fridays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-heading=&quot;Learn how we think&quot;&gt;Learn how we think&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;external-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e8HplJ2Ief4&amp;amp;t=8s&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-tooltip-position=&quot;top&quot;&gt;The $40M push to modernize fleet payments&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;podcast with our founder and CEO, Daniel Simon&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;external-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.iconiq.com/growth/insights/fueling-the-financial-operating-system-for-fleets-our-partnership-with-coast&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-tooltip-position=&quot;top&quot;&gt;Fueling the Financial Operating System for Fleets: Our Partnership with Coast&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;ICONIQ Series B blog post&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is Coast&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coast is re-imagining the trillion-dollar U.S. B2B card payments infrastructure, with a focus on the country’s 500,000 commercial fleets, 40 million commercial vehicles, and many millions of commercial drivers. The incumbent technologies that cater to these customers are decades old, and businesses with fleets increasingly demand modern digital experiences and transparent financial services products. Coast’s mission is to deliver this at a transformational scale, beginning with the Coast Fleet and Fuel Card built on a cutting-edge spend management platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Staff Data Engineer who can not just get their hands dirty building pipelines and also act as a thought leader for the company. Data sits at the center of everything we do, and we need someone who not only understands how to make it available, but how to make it accessible to everyone in the company. In the age of AI, making good decisions is key, and having accurate data is a core part of our decision-making process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You won&#39;t be starting from scratch. We already run on Redshift, Dagster, and dbt, but the biggest pieces are still yours to build: a data catalog, a semantic layer, a mature security posture, and AI-ready access to our data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a chance to lead a small, high-leverage team and touch all corners of the company, not just reporting and analytics. Our data organization follows a federated model: product teams own their data products, and the data platform gives them the patterns, tools, and guardrails to do that well. Your job isn&#39;t to be the team everyone files tickets with; it&#39;s to make everyone else at Coast better at producing and using data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Our Data Warehouse&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set standards and build patterns for ingesting data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure data consumers can build models efficiently and quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build new capabilities, like data catalogs and semantic layers that make data discoverable for your coworkers across the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set data security standards, including tokenization, RBAC, and row-level security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide High-Quality Patterns&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You should have opinions, we want you to be the expert on the best way to produce and consume data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Figure out how to make data usable, whether via reverse ETL or making it available to AI agents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a Teacher&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help our product engineering teams evolve from treating data as exhaust to building DDD-based data products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teach nontechnical users how to consume data using AI tools without needing to learn SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evangelize new practices and patterns that present opportunities for Coast to remain innovative and nimble&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Write Code&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to our data pipelines in Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build CI/CD pipelines for data products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute new data tests for dbt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your first year, you’ll be successful if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide a model for understanding our data warehouse costs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship a data catalog that helps all employees know where to find good data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a strategy and have made real progress on building a data security posture, including row-level security, RBAC, and tokenization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a strategy and have made real progress on making our data safely accessible to AI agents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years hands-on experience working across the data ecosystem, from modern ETL/ELT and orchestration to data warehouses and columnar stores, from BI tooling for less-technical business users to SQL optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native mindset: you’re already using AI tools in your daily work and you’re excited to push further&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data warehouses such as Redshift or Snowflake (we use Redshift), data pipeline tools (we use Dagster), dbt, and medallion architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a horizontal Data Engineering team, working with analytics and product engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentorship experience, both of data engineers and members of other teams who have to touch data products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bias toward action and process-building; you don’t wait for someone to hand you a playbook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in ambiguity; you can build structure where none exists without losing momentum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New York City based; able to be in-office 3–4 days per week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our salary ranges are based on paying competitively for our size and industry, and are one part of our total compensation package that also includes benefits and equity. Pay decisions are based on a number of factors, including scope and qualifications for the role, experience level, skillset, and balancing internal equity relative to other Coast employees. We expect the majority of candidates who are offered roles at Coast to fall healthily within the range based on these factors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary range&lt;/strong&gt;: $170,000 – $220,000 annually&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity Grant&lt;/strong&gt;: Meaningful potential upside given Coast’s early-stage trajectory&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits Overview&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental and vision insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible paid time off (vacation, personal well being, paid holidays)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tools to help manage your financial wellness, including webinars, access to an equity tax advisory service, and company-sponsored 401(k)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$400 accessories allowance (a keyboard, mouse, headphones, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free lunch every Friday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coast is committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion. We are building a diverse and inclusive environment, so we encourage people of all backgrounds to apply. We’re an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, disability, national origin, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable federal, state, or local law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check out the latest podcast interview on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fintechoneonone.com/financial-platform-physical-economy-daniel-simon-coast/&quot;&gt;Fintech One on One with Coast Founder Daniel Simon&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fintechlayercake.buzzsprout.com/1985266/14997028-fleet-card-masterclass-with-coast-founder-daniel-simon&quot;&gt;!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Coast, is building the smart financial infrastructure powering America&#39;s fleets. AI is fundamentally changing how fleets run their financial operations, and we&#39;re shaping the tools this new era requires.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2020, Coast has become the payments and expense management platform of choice for the 500,000 fleets and 40 million vehicles that keep the country moving by giving fleet owners and operators control, visibility, and trust over how their businesses spend.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In an industry where complexity is the norm, we&#39;re building something simple yet opinionated and focused: software that field owners, managers, and workers actually want to use. Every member of our fully co-located team is a builder who demonstrates high agency, ownership, and urgency every day. We also care deeply about bringing modern, well-crafted tools to the trades; an industry that&#39;s been underserved for too long. This mindset drives everything we do, from product decisions to hiring choices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Product Designer, you are accountable for business outcomes, not just design quality and customer delight. You work with product managers, engineers, and other designers to define the right problems, explore and validate solutions, and ship product experiences that change customer behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design at Coast is AI first and builder-led. Work starts in an LLM, moves into tools like Claude Code, Cursor, and Codex to explore flows and interactions, and then comes into Figma for systems and polish. Designers prototype early, test with real customers, and stay involved through launch and iteration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for multiple product designers who are excited to work this way and who want to use AI as a core part of how they design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Location &amp;amp; work mode&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coast is an in-person company. This role is based out of our New York City office and requires in-person presence 3 to 4 days a week. We believe great products are built by people who are in the room together: collaborating closely, moving fast, and holding each other to a high bar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-end product ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Pair closely with product managers and engineers to define problems, explore solutions, validate concepts, and ship improvements and new capabilities that move key business metrics. Stay involved through launch and iteration, not just handoff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer research &amp;amp; validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Talk directly with customers to uncover needs and validate assumptions, leverage LLMs to synthesize insights and identify patterns, and run quick tests to refine solutions. Treat research as a tool to accelerate decisions, not a gate to progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prototyping &amp;amp; development:&lt;/strong&gt; Use AI-powered tools to build functional prototypes, work directly with code, and ship UI improvements to production in collaboration with engineers, without compromising design craft, code quality, or user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design for simplicity:&lt;/strong&gt; Encode complexity into intuitive experiences that make the right actions easy and the default path successful for most customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous product quality improvement:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactively identify and fix usability issues, design inconsistencies, and everyday “paper cuts” across Coast, using AI-powered development tools to ship improvements directly to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Elevate design craft &amp;amp; quality:&lt;/strong&gt; Champion great design across Coast through thoughtful critique and collaboration. Share AI techniques, best practices, and learnings with fellow designers, and continuously improve our design system to raise the bar for consistency, usability, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring:&lt;/strong&gt; Help with hiring and onboarding and new teammates that can elevate our team and product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 6 years of experience as a product designer working on complex products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio that shows strong product thinking and design craft (i.e., interaction design, visual design, information architecture, ux writing, and user research)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to distill problems and feedback, then design clear, focused solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Courage to ask questions, experiment, and advocate for what you feel is right&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Humility to accept feedback, adapt your thinking, and iterate toward the best solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active use of LLMs (e.g., Claude, ChatGPT) in your design workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex even if you are not writing production code by hand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with product managers to define success metrics and iterate based on results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective written and verbal communication skills, and comfort collaborating directly with product managers and engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we offer&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll have a high-impact role with real ownership and the opportunity to shape the future of Coast’s products and services&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary ($205,000—$230,000 USD) and equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-sponsored 401(k)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible paid time off (vacation, personal well being, paid holidays)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$400 accessories allowance (a keyboard, mouse, headphones, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tools to help manage your financial wellness, including webinar, and access to an equity tax advisory service&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free lunch on Fridays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
